        <mxCell id="c15" value="&lt;b&gt;The drill-through click&lt;/b&gt; The Drillthrough option of the right-click menu, the filters a click passes and the back button, which responds only with Ctrl held&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Tutorial&amp;nbsp;15.1, Steps&amp;nbsp;7 and 9; Tutorial&amp;nbsp;15.2, Step&amp;nbsp;8; Exercise&amp;nbsp;15.1&lt;/i&gt;" style="rounded=0;arcSize=6;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FEF5E7;strokeColor=#8A5D00;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#2C3E50;fontSize=13;fontStyle=0;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="438" y="40" width="422" height="86" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c16" value="&lt;b&gt;The visual calculations&lt;/b&gt; The YTD and Change columns of Exercise&amp;nbsp;15.2, the RUNNINGSUM of Tutorial&amp;nbsp;15.2, Step&amp;nbsp;10 and the moving average of Tutorial&amp;nbsp;15.3, Steps&amp;nbsp;8 and 9. They are computed inside the visual, so no row of the Checks tab can read them: compare them by eye&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Tutorial&amp;nbsp;15.2; Tutorial&amp;nbsp;15.3; Exercise&amp;nbsp;15.2&lt;/i&gt;" style="rounded=0;arcSize=6;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FEF5E7;strokeColor=#8A5D00;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#2C3E50;fontSize=13;fontStyle=0;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="438" y="134" width="422" height="102" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c17" value="&lt;b&gt;The field-parameter slicer&lt;/b&gt; Whether the slicer changes the measure the chart shows, and what Desktop does when the parameter is tried as a drill-through field&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Exercise&amp;nbsp;15.3, Requirements 3 and 5&lt;/i&gt;" style="rounded=0;arcSize=6;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FEF5E7;strokeColor=#8A5D00;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#2C3E50;fontSize=13;fontStyle=0;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="438" y="244" width="422" height="86" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c18" value="&lt;b&gt;The Analytics-pane forecast&lt;/b&gt; Desktop computes it, and a new release can move it: grade the audit note, not the value&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Exercise&amp;nbsp;15.5&lt;/i&gt;" style="rounded=0;arcSize=6;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FEF5E7;strokeColor=#8A5D00;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#2C3E50;fontSize=13;fontStyle=0;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="438" y="338" width="422" height="70" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c19" value="&lt;i&gt;The Checks tab of the model answer holds 268 rows for the tutorials and exercises of the chapter (383 with the sections of Chapters 13 and 14). Choose Home &gt; Refresh, then Run. A row tests a value, not how a visual looks, so the right-hand column is for the instructor to open the pages.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5D6D7E;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="560" width="860" height="38" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
